## 1. Proprietary Software & Original Derivations

All application source code, user interface designs, frontend and backend architectures, database schemas, CBT pacing engines, spaced-repetition algorithms, and all original pedagogical derivations, step-by-step mathematical proofs, distractor analyses, and examiner notes authored by the Qelem Development Team are proprietary software and intellectual property of the Qelem Development Team.

Unauthorized copying, modification, decompilation, redistribution, commercial exploitation, or public mirroring of this software codebase is strictly prohibited without prior written authorization from the copyright holders.

---

## 2. Third-Party Examination Content & Rights Notice

Third-party national examination questions, historical examination prompts, and official curriculum syllabi referenced within this platform are sourced from public past examination papers originally published by the Ethiopian national examination authorities:

- **Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia (FDRE) Ministry of Education**
- **Educational Assessment and Examinations Service (EAES)** (formerly National Educational Assessment and Examinations Agency / NEAEA)

**Current Rights Status:** The formal rights status and authorization for digital curation of these public past examination papers is currently **under active review** with the appropriate educational authorities. Qelem claims no ownership over official examination questions, syllabi structures, or national answer keys.

---

## 3. Strict Prohibition on Question Bank Redistribution

No redistribution, automated harvesting, scraping, bulk export, commercial resale, or unauthorized sublicensing of the curated question bank, LaTeX mathematical formatting, or digital exam papers is permitted.

Individual students and educators may access the platform solely for personal, non-commercial academic study and examination preparation.
